Id: fsys017w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_names
Controls: NIST SI-4; ISO 8.16

Files with unusual names (see fsys005a) were found in a directory where
such names are routine rather than suspicious: home directories, media
and backup disks, and copies of other systems' files. Apple's resource
fork files ("._name"), mail index files ("..cmeta") and browser lock
files are the usual culprits. Tiger reports how many and where instead
of listing each one. The directories where each file is still listed
individually (fsys005a) are set by Tiger_FSScan_DetailDirs in tigerrc;
set it to '*' to list them all.
